<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT color=#0000ff size=6&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=5 face=Arial&gt;MSR Base Station In-band General Blocking&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;This example demonstrates how to measure the MSR base station in-band selectivity and blocking according to clause&amp;nbsp;7.4 of 3GPP TS 37.141.&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 9pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;The in-band selectivity and blocking characteristics are measures of the receiver ability to receive a wanted signal at its assigned channel in the presence of an unwanted interferer inside the operating band and are defined by a wideband and a narrowband blocking requirement. This example tests the wideband blocking requirement. T&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 11pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Calibri&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: &#x00E5;&#x00AE;&#x008B;&#x00E4;&#x00BD;&#x0093;; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: ZH-CN; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA&quot;&gt;he interfering signal shall be a UTRA FDD signal.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;In this example,&amp;nbsp;one GSM carrier and one WCDMA carrier from MSR Band 8 (880MHz - 915MHz) are combined using SingalCombiner part. The interfering signal is a UTRA FDD signal. The MSR bands definition can be found in Table 4.4-1 of 3GPP TS 37.104.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;Equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt; specifies the used MSR Band and the signal configurations of each carrier e.g. sampling rate and bandwidth.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;The spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power&quot; shows the combined spectrum, while the spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power with individual spectrums&quot; shows the combined spectrum along with individual standard spectrum.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;Table &quot;BER&quot; shows the measured bit error rate of each carrier.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;TRY THIS:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;Change MSR bands in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt; by setting F_BWlow, F_BWhigh and F_BWmid.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;Change the interferer configuraiton in equation T&lt;EM&gt;estConfiguration.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;Change the wanted signal configuration in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Arial&gt;Sweep the &lt;EM&gt;FreqOffsetStep &lt;/EM&gt;of the interferer signal with step size 1MHz using &quot;Sweep1&quot;.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
